From: Keenetic SDK Builder <developers@keenetic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: initialise the header protection rwsem in wg_newlink

wg_newlink() initialises every other lock in struct wg_device but never
touches wg->header_protection.lock, so the rwsem stays as alloc_netdev()
left it: all zeroes. awg_has_header_protection() then takes it on the
very first `awg set`/`setconf`.

With CONFIG_RWSEM_XCHGADD_ALGORITHM (aarch64) a zeroed rwsem happens to
read as unlocked and the bug is invisible. With
CONFIG_RWSEM_GENERIC_SPINLOCK (every 4.9-ndm MIPS target) __down_read()
tests list_empty(&sem->wait_list) on a list_head whose next/prev are
NULL, decides there are waiters, and dereferences NULL in list_add_tail:

  CPU 3 Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 00000000
  epc   : __down_read+0x94/0x110
  [<...>] awg_has_header_protection+0x20/0x44 [amneziawg]
  [<...>] wg_set_device+0x50/0x9a4 [amneziawg]

Reproduced on KN-1810 (mt7621, 4.9-ndm-5): one `awg setconf` on a freshly
created amneziawg interface reboots the router, which is the mipsel
bootloop reported downstream. Upstream is unfixed as of v3.0.20260731-04.

Signed-off-by: Keenetic SDK Builder <developers@keenetic.com>
---
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -372,6 +372,7 @@
 
 	rcu_assign_pointer(wg->creating_net, link_net);
 	init_rwsem(&wg->static_identity.lock);
+	init_rwsem(&wg->header_protection.lock);
 	mutex_init(&wg->socket_update_lock);
 	mutex_init(&wg->device_update_lock);
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(wg->ispecs); ++i)
